---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
type DriverRow = { id: string; state_code: string; office: string; components_pp: Record<string, number>;
	reported_comparison: { baseline_year?: number; reported_change_pp: number | null;
		other_and_unallocated_pp: number | null; baseline_alignment_pp: number | null } };
const data = JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/participation-return-attribution/20261110-02/viewer-data.json', 'utf8'));
const receipt = JSON.parse(readFileSync('data/participation-return-attribution/20261110-02/download.json', 'utf8'));
const payload = JSON.stringify({ data, names }).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c');
const pp = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable' : `${value > 0 ? '+' : ''}${value.toFixed(2)}`;
---
<section id="participation-return-drivers" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="return-drivers-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">2026 · Reported swing and modeled contributions</p>
		<h2 id="return-drivers-title">What moved the margin?</h2>
		<p>Compare the <strong>reported swing</strong> with modeled switching, modeled nonparticipation,
			and the remaining other or unallocated change. Select an office, then a state on any map.</p>
	</header>
	<p class="caption">Reported swing compares qualified earlier <strong>same-office returns</strong>;
		the year and source frame are shown for each state. Margin = 100 × (D − R) / (D + R).
		“Staying home” is modeled nonparticipation, not a confirmed missing ballot.</p>
	<div class="driver-controls">
		<label>2026 office<select data-driver-office disabled><option value="house">House · states</option>
			<option value="senate">Senate</option><option value="governor">Governor · frames</option></select></label>
		<label>State<select data-driver-state disabled><option value="">Loading state context…</option></select></label>
	</div>
	<p data-driver-status class="caption" role="status">Saved 2026 model estimates. The full numerical table works without JavaScript.</p>
	<div data-driver-summary class="driver-summary" hidden aria-live="polite"></div>
	<div class="driver-maps">
		<section class="driver-map-card" aria-labelledby="driver-total-map-title">
			<h3 id="driver-total-map-title">Reported swing</h3>
			<p class="caption">Total same-office change in the known-D/R margin.</p>
			<div class="driver-map" data-driver-map="reported_total"></div>
		</section>
		<section class="driver-map-card" aria-labelledby="driver-switch-map-title">
			<h3 id="driver-switch-map-title">Switching sides</h3>
			<p class="caption">Contribution from changing between major-party choices.</p>
			<div class="driver-map" data-driver-map="switching"></div>
		</section>
		<section class="driver-map-card" aria-labelledby="driver-nonparticipation-map-title">
			<h3 id="driver-nonparticipation-map-title">Staying home · modeled</h3>
			<p class="caption">Contribution from model-classified nonparticipation.</p>
			<div class="driver-map" data-driver-map="modeled_nonparticipation"></div>
		</section>
		<section class="driver-map-card" aria-labelledby="driver-other-map-title">
			<h3 id="driver-other-map-title">Other / unallocated</h3>
			<p class="caption">Reported total minus the two modeled effects; not one mechanism.</p>
			<div class="driver-map" data-driver-map="other_and_unallocated"></div>
		</section>
	</div>
	<div class="driver-map-key" aria-label="Shared signed margin-point scale">
		<div><div class="driver-map-ramp"></div><div class="driver-map-ticks">
			<span data-driver-scale-min></span><span>0</span><span data-driver-scale-max></span>
		</div><div class="driver-map-directions"><span>Republican direction</span><span>Democratic direction</span></div></div>
		<span class="driver-no-model"><i></i>No qualified comparison / model</span>
	</div>
	<p class="caption driver-map-note">Colour shows <strong>signed percentage-point changes or contributions to the margin</strong>,
		not party vote shares or turnout rates. Reported total = switching + modeled nonparticipation + other / unallocated.
		No state estimate is spread onto counties or precincts.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Selected state: full accounting and source qualifications</summary>
		<div data-driver-detail class="driver-detail" hidden></div>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>How to read these estimates and their uncertainty</summary>
	<p class="caption">The selected state's ranges vary switching/nonparticipation contrast strength from 0.5× to 1.5×.
		They are <strong>partial assumption sensitivity, not confidence intervals</strong>.
		The gap can be larger than either modeled effect; it is not assigned to people switching or staying home.
		Model-classified nonparticipation is not administrative evidence of no ballot. D.C. has no NORC sample.</p>
	<p class="caption">NORC participation information and candidate returns constrain the model.
		The original seven modeled terms compare recalled presidential choice in the current survey frame.
		A separate unallocated baseline-alignment term bridges them to the reported same-office swing;
		these original terms are not fitted to the earlier partisan result.
		55 office-specific switching tables are used; other office terms require explicit transport assumptions.
		Entry, other choices, unknowns, denominator changes and the unallocated return/frame gap are retained.
		These are conditional estimates, not causal persuasion. No state survey model is assigned to counties or precincts.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Every saved estimate and full accounting</summary>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All 113 saved modeled effect estimates">
			<table><caption>Reported same-office swing and original model-frame terms; signed margin points. Unavailable is not zero.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">State / office</th><th scope="col">Switching</th><th scope="col">Nonparticipation</th>
					<th scope="col">Entry</th><th scope="col">Other</th><th scope="col">Unknown</th>
					<th scope="col">Denominator</th><th scope="col">Current-frame gap</th>
					<th scope="col">Prior-office year</th><th scope="col">Reported swing</th>
					<th scope="col">Other / unallocated total</th><th scope="col">Baseline alignment</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{data.rows.map((row: DriverRow) =>
					<tr data-saved-driver={row.id}><th scope="row">{names[row.state_code]} · {row.office}</th>
						{['switching', 'modeled_nonparticipation', 'no_prior_contest_vote_entry',
							'other_choice', 'unresolved', 'denominator', 'return_frame_gap'].map(key =>
							<td class="numeric">{pp(row.components_pp[key])}</td>)}
						<td>{row.reported_comparison.baseline_year ?? 'Unavailable'}</td>
						{['reported_change_pp', 'other_and_unallocated_pp', 'baseline_alignment_pp'].map(key =>
							<td class="numeric">{pp(row.reported_comparison[key as 'reported_change_pp'])}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links"><a href={receipt.url}>Complete historical returns, inputs, all models/scenarios, code and checksums · ZIP</a></div>
	<script type="application/json" is:inline data-driver-data set:html={payload}></script>
</section>
<script>
	import { initializeReturnDrivers } from '../../public/scripts/participation-return-drivers.js';
	initializeReturnDrivers();
</script>
<style>
	#participation-return-drivers { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
	.driver-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.3fr);
		gap: .75rem; margin-block: 1.25rem .75rem; max-width: 45rem; }
	.driver-controls label { display: grid; min-width: 0; gap: .3rem; font: .73rem var(--sans); }
	.driver-controls :is(select,input) { width: 100%; min-width: 0; padding: .5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: inherit; }
	.driver-maps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap: 2rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
	.driver-map-card { min-width: 0; }
	.driver-map-card h3 { margin: 0 0 .35rem; font: 400 1.3rem var(--serif); }
	.driver-map-card > p { margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
	.driver-map { min-height: 120px; }
	.driver-map :global(svg) { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-state) { stroke: var(--paper); stroke-width: .8; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke; cursor: pointer; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-state:hover), .driver-map :global(.driver-state.selected) { stroke: #243f49; stroke-width: 1.8; }
	.driver-map :global(.driver-inset-label) { fill: var(--muted); font: 15px var(--sans); }
	.driver-map-key { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
		gap: .5rem .75rem; font: .66rem/1.4 var(--sans); color: var(--muted); margin-block: .75rem; }
	.driver-map-key > div { width: min(100%, 20rem); }
	.driver-map-ramp { height: .5rem; background: linear-gradient(to right,#a47045,#f1eee6,#2c6c75); }
	.driver-map-ticks { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .25rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	.driver-map-directions { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: .25rem; }
	.driver-no-model { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; margin-left: .5rem; }
	.driver-no-model i { width: .65rem; height: .65rem; background: #d6d3cb; }
	.driver-map-note { max-width: 85ch; margin-inline: auto; }
	.driver-detail { margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: .5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); min-width: 0; }
	.driver-summary { margin-block: 1rem; padding-block: .75rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.driver-summary :global(h3) { margin: 0 0 .4rem; font: 400 1.15rem var(--serif); }
	.driver-summary :global(p) { margin: .4rem 0; }
	.driver-summary :global(.driver-equation) { font: .85rem/1.65 var(--sans); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	@media(max-width:760px) {
		.driver-maps { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr); gap: 1.25rem; }
		.driver-map-key { justify-content: flex-start; }
		.driver-map-key > div { width: 100%; }
		.driver-no-model { flex-basis: 100%; margin-left: 0; }
	}
</style>
